        505.8451232910156,
        331.46533203125,
        521.5771484375
      ],
      "text": "living with HIV in settings with a high TB burden",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        528.7850341796875,
        527.3806762695312,
        543.22802734375
      ],
      "text": "TB is the main cause of hospitalization and mortality among people living with HIV. The assessment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        541.9849853515625,
        527.4652709960938,
        556.427978515625
      ],
      "text": "of the performance of an mWRD used as a combined TB screening and diagnostic strategy for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        555.1851196289062,
        527.3892822265625,
        569.6281127929688
      ],
      "text": "medical ward patients with HIV included 4 studies in Ghana, Myanmar and South Africa with a total",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        568.2750244140625,
        527.4086303710938,
        582.8280029296875
      ],
      "text": "Web Annex B Web Annex C of 639 participants (see  , Table 15, and  , Table 8). The prevalence of TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        581.5850219726562,
        527.4213256835938,
        596.0280151367188
      ],
      "text": "in the included studies was 23.8%, ranging from 7% to 26%. The mWRD test assessed in the IPD was",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        594.7850341796875,
        229.88223266601562,
        609.22802734375
      ],
      "text": "primarily the Xpert MTB/RIF assay.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        616.4888916015625,
        527.2527465820312,
        630.931884765625
      ],
      "text": "Using the W4SS alone had 96% sensitivity and 11% specificity in the IPD meta-analysis of medical ward",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.961231231689453,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        629.6890258789062,
        527.3883666992188,
        644.1320190429688
      ],
      "text": "inpatients living with HIV, 94% of whom were positive on the W4SS. Thus, the difference in accuracy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        642.8890380859375,
        527.532958984375,
        657.33203125
      ],
      "text": "was minimal between the full screening and diagnostic strategy of using W4SS followed by mWRD and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.957568168640137,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        656.0889892578125,
        527.3927001953125,
        670.531982421875
      ],
      "text": "using mWRD alone. Therefore, the value of the W4SS was judged to have limited utility in screening",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        669.2890014648438,
        527.3926391601562,
        683.7319946289062
      ],
      "text": "for TB in this population prior to an mWRD test, and the GDG recommended that medical inpatients",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        682.4888916015625,
        527.4520263671875,
        696.931884765625
      ],
      "text": "should be screened and tested with an mWRD, irrespective of symptoms, to inform a decision about",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        695.6890258789062,
        527.3971557617188,
        710.1320190429688
      ],
      "text": "whether to treat for TB. A 10% threshold TB prevalence among hospital inpatients living with HIV is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        708.8890380859375,
        527.4411010742188,
        723.33203125
      ],
      "text": "recommended, taking into account the TB prevalence among the participants studied and striking",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        722.0889892578125,
        527.5870971679688,
        736.531982421875
      ],
      "text": "a balance between ensuring rapid diagnosis in this critically ill population and the need to avoid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        735.2890014648438,
        527.433349609375,
        749.7319946289062
      ],
      "text": "overtreatment. In lower prevalence settings, a screening and diagnostic strategy with mWRD alone",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        748.4888916015625,
        527.4376831054688,
        762.931884765625
      ],
      "text": "would give rise to higher numbers of false positives, with overtreatment and the related social and",
